            "outcome": {
                "name": "Oral and topical hydrogen administration for 2 weeks in male professional athletes with acute soft tissue injuries augmented plasma viscosity decrease and enhanced recovery of joint flexibility compared to traditional treatment alone. No significant differences were found for CRP, IL-6, pain scores, or limb swelling, but range of motion recovery was faster with hydrogen. Mild diarrhea was reported in two participants; no serious adverse events occurred.",
